    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001XQ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (in Communication Sciences and Child Language Disorders) (E&L) (26001XQ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (in Communication Sciences and Child Language Disorders) (E&L) (26001XQ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (in Communication Sciences and Child Language Disorders) (E&L) (26001XQ) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Education and Langauges: Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (in Communication Sciences and Child Language Disorders) (E&L) - ( 26001XQ ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : School of Education and Languages Closing Date : 14/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible for the following major duties and responsibilities: teaching and coordinating postgraduate and undergraduate courses; developing curriculum in line with current research and professional standards; supervising student projects and clinical practicum and placements where appropriate; conducting high-quality research and publishing in reputable international journals; contributing to programme administration, programme promotion, student advising, and quality assurance activities; and engaging in professional and community outreach, including collaboration with healthcare, educational and community partners. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: a doctoral degree in Communication Disorders, Educational Psychology, Linguistics, or a closely related discipline; demonstrate specialization in one or more of the following areas: child language disorders, speech disorders, reading and writing difficulties, or/and counselling skills for communicative disorders; fluency in English and Mandarin Chinese, with demonstrated ability to teach and communicate effectively in both languages; a strong commitment to high-quality teaching at the postgraduate level and to student supervision; and good interpersonal skills, the ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team, and a strong sense of responsibility and professionalism. Preference will be given to candidates who meet one or more of the following criteria: fluency in Cantonese, particularly with experience serving Cantonese-speaking children; a strong track record of research publications in high-impact journals and demonstrated potential for securing competitive external research funding; professional qualifications such as Registered Speech Therapist or Educational Psychologist in Hong Kong or an equivalent jurisdiction; and relevant clinical and/or educational experience in communication disorders, inclusive education, or related areas in school, healthcare, or community settings. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young T eaching Staff ” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust” Overseas candidates who are successfully appointed by the University and below age 50 will be eligible to apply for the “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust”.  This programme offers the opportunity to reside in assigned accommodation free of charge for a period of up to six months, subject to terms and conditions. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in Jul 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WU": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant II – Unreal Developer (R7073) (A&SS) (26001WU)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant II – Unreal Developer (R7073) (A&SS) (26001WU) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant II – Unreal Developer (R7073) (A&SS) (26001WU) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Arts and Social Sciences : Research Assistant II – Unreal Developer (R7073) (A&SS) - ( 26001WU ) Job : Full-time R&D School/Unit : Wu Jieh Yee School of Arts and Social Sciences Closing Date : 26/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointees shall mainly assist the research team in a research project “ Reimagining the Classics of Chinese Literature: Immersive Experiences of Eileen Chang’s Literary World and Classical Travel Narratives ” (Project No.: R7073). The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Constructing 2D/3D assets for the use of the research project; Designing and developing immersive experience using Unreal; Researching and developing novel 2D/3D visualization and interaction experience with Chinese literature and culture for large-scale immersive display space; Assisting the Principal Investigator/supervisors to prepare experiments; and Conducting other ad-hoc research activities as instructed by the Principal Investigator. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A Bachelor’s degree or above in Creative/Interactive Media, Computer Science, or any related disciplines; Intermediate knowledge of and practical experience with Unreal Engine development, Blueprint scripting, and C++ programming; Understanding interactive 3D simulation in virtual / augmented reality or generative AI would be an advantage; Fresh graduates are welcome, and candidates who have intention to pursue a research postgraduate degree are preferable; Detail-oriented, hardworking, responsible, self-motivated, able to meet deadlines and work independently; and Excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary and an end-of-contract gratuity will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. Please indicate your expected salary. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled"
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001XC": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Academic Service Manager (REG) (26001XC)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Academic Service Manager (REG) (26001XC) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Academic Service Manager (REG) (26001XC) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . The Registry is a key central administrative unit of the University supporting it in providing quality higher education. We administer and deliver a broad range of student and academic services, such as admissions, registration, quality assurance, class scheduling, examinations, and graduation. The Registry is also responsible for maintaining student records and providing secretarial support to Senate and its committees, and are integral in the governing of academic regulations of the University. We provide aspiring candidates with ample staff development opportunities and a promising career in higher education. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Registry : Assistant Academic Service Manager (REG) - ( 26001XC ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Registry Closing Date : 13/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Leading a small team of supporting staff in provision of effective administrative services and support in class scheduling & tutors matters; Handling class scheduling & accommodation booking for programmes/courses, and tutors matters for part-time programmes; Driving continuous enhancements and streamlining of timetabling processes; Compiling statistical reports and conducting estimations and analyses to support decision-making; Assisting in practice review & implementation, system testing and enhancement; Providing executive to committee work; and Supervising junior/clerical staff, and performining any other tasks as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized degree with at least 2 years’ relevant post-qualification administrative and supervisory experience; Excellent interpersonal and communication skills in both English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; Strong analytical mindset, with excellent organizational abilities; Attentive to details and proactive problem-solving; Proficiency in computer applications; and Ability to manage multiple tasks concurrently while working effectively under pressure and meeting tight schedules. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001X6": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Multimedia Technology Manager (ALTO) (26001X6) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Multimedia Technology Manager (ALTO) (26001X6) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in Office for Advancement of Learning and Teaching (ALTO) : Senior Multimedia Technology Manager (ALTO) - ( 26001X6 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office for Advancement of Learning and Teaching Closing Date : 10/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Taking the lead to implement new initiatives by applying the latest technologies, including Artificial Intelligence (AI) in learning and teaching; Overseeing the design, development, enhancement and maintenance of AI Systems; Evaluating software development lifecycle processes, workflows, standards, and quality-assurance practices; Designing system architectures, configuring and managing servers and cloud infrastructure; Managing the procurement and tendering of IT hardware, software, and cloud services; Supervising Managers and Systems Analysts, and monitoring their assigned tasks; Conducting in-house training and assisting in the provision of professional development for University staff; Undertaking other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of the Office for Advancement of Learning and Teaching and his/her nominees. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized bachelor's degree in Computer Science Artificial Intelligence, or a related discipline. At least 10 years' relevant post-qualification experience in IT project management and application development, preferably in higher education institutions; In-depth knowledge of modern web technologies, including Python, Node.js, TypeScript, Vue.js/React, relational databases (PostgreSQL, MySQL), LMS platforms, and AI applications; Strong expertise in driving AI applications and integration strategy, with practical experience in leveraging LLMs, Machine Learning technologies, and modern AI frameworks to solve academic/institutional problems. Strong leadership in vendor management, budget planning, IT governance, and system integration across cross-functional teams; Strong project management skills, communication skills, supervisory skills, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate academic/institutional requirements into technical solutions . Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
