      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Manager/ Officer (Mainland) (Mainland and International Affairs) (26001WL)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Manager/ Officer (Mainland) (Mainland and International Affairs) (26001WL) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Manager/ Officer (Mainland) (Mainland and International Affairs) (26001WL) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Mainland and International Affairs Office. Assistant Manager/ Officer (Mainland) (Mainland and International Affairs) - ( 26001WL ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Mainland and International Affairs Office Closing Date : 09/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Supporting Chinese Mainland Student Recruitment: Analyse recruitment data, monitor market trends and competitor strategies, and track policy developments to inform evidence-based recruitment decisions Assist in sourcing and evaluating potential student recruitment opportunities across the Chinese Mainland Support the execution of the Chinese Mainland student recruitment plan, contributing to the recruitment pipeline that leads to the enrolment of mainland students at the University; and Assist in developing and refining processes to ensure efficient and effective resolution of recruitment-related enquiries Admissions Operations Support: Assist in the day-to-day management of admissions operations, ensuring the smooth and timely processing of applications Support the implementation of admissions procedures and workflows under the guidance of senior staff; and Provide operational support throughout the admissions journey to help retain and convert strong candidates Supporting Management on External Engagements: Provide support to management regarding HKMU's external engagements, including assisting with the coordination of incoming visits from partner institutions and higher education organisations from Chinese mainland, as well as supporting student mobility missions Providing executive and administrative support to the Mainland and International Affairs Office; and Performing any other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Manager or Director of Mainland and International Affairs. Candidates with less experience and/or low qualification may be considered for post of Officer. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized Bachelor's degree; a background in Education, Communications, Marketing, or a related discipline is preferred At least 3 years of relevant working experience; prior experience in mainland student recruitment, educational promotion, or cross-border collaborative projects is an advantage A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, proficiency in Mandarin is a MUST Familiarity with the mainland education system and admission policies, with an understanding of the tertiary education needs of students across different provinces and cities Strong communication, coordination, and organizational skills, with a strong team spirit Ability to work independently and willingness to travel to Chinese mainland cities; and Proficiency in office software applications (e.g., Word, Excel, PowerPoint) Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WG": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Officer (International) (Mainland and International Affairs) (26001WG) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Officer (International) (Mainland and International Affairs) (26001WG) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Mainland and International Affairs Office. Officer (International) (Mainland and International Affairs) - ( 26001WG ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Mainland and International Affairs Office Closing Date : 09/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of the Mainland and International Affairs Office (MIAO) or his/her nominee(s), the appointee will support the team and its international student recruitment activities. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Managing international student recruitment administration, including but not limited to day-to-day operations of the recruitment pipeline, handling inquiries from international applicants, and undertaking document checking and preparation related to scholarship nomination and administration Coordinating with internal and external stakeholders, particularly central units and academic schools at HKMU, to ensure effective communication and collaboration in support of recruitment efforts Implementing targeted student recruitment plans for priority regions in the international market to meet enrolment targets; travel outside normal office hours may be required Assisting in the analysis of application and admissions data to support the preparation of relevant reports Performing other duties as assigned by the Director of MIAO or his/her nominee(s) Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised Bachelor’s degree, preferably in business-related discipline At least 2 years of relevant experience in full-time programme administration or project management within the tertiary education sector A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua Strong communication, coordination, and organizational skills, with a strong team spirit Proficiency in office software applications (e.g., Word, Excel, PowerPoint) Study abroad experience is preferred Shortlisted candidates invited to attend a written test and an interview. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WQ": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Student Services Officer (SOL) (26001WQ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Student Services Officer (SOL) (26001WQ) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Open Learning : Student Services Officer (SOL) - ( 26001WQ ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : School of Open Learning Closing Date : 08/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Assisting in planning and executing comprehensive social media and digital marketing strategies, to maximize the awareness of the School and its programmes; Monitoring digital campaign performance against KPIs, leveraging advanced analytics and market trends, and delivering campaign effectiveness analysis; Executing student recruitment activities by supporting school promotion activities, including roadshows, expos, and networking events to strengthen audience connection; Identifying new platforms, tools, partnerships, and market opportunities to enhance school visibility and student acquisition; Liaising with internal and external parties to ensure that the school activities, services and programmes pertaining to distance-learning and part-time students’ learning and support are effectively provided; and Performing any other duties as assigned. The appointee may be required to work occasionally outside normal office hours, including weekday evenings, Saturdays and Sundays. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree, preferably with 3 years post-qualification working experience in digital marketing, CRM system management and event management; Extensive knowledge of the digital marketing landscape, with a strong proficiency in using various digital media platforms (such as Youtube, Meta Ads, Google Ads) and familiar with the social media operation strategies in Hong Kong; Experience in a marketing agency is an advantage, a good understanding and network connection in the educational landscape will be a plus; Strong problem-solving skills, with a proactive approach in managing multiple priorities effectively and an ability to work independently under tight deadlines; A good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese and Putonghua; and Proficient PC skills, including MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint and the use of AI tools. Applicants may provide any of their marketing campaign portfolios in the application. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WS": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Human Resources Officer (HRO) (26001WS)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Human Resources Officer (HRO) (26001WS) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Human Resources Officer (HRO) (26001WS) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Human Resources O ffice : Assistant Human Resources Officer (HRO) - ( 26001WS ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Human Resources Office Closing Date : 09/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: providing support in specialised HR functional areas such as systems, C&B, performance management, talent cultivation, engagement & development, appointment, staff regulations, strategic initiatives and manpower planning; providing one-stop HR service to Schools/Offices; providing support to meetings and committee work; maintaining accurate and up-to-date human resources records; and compiling HR-related management statistics and reports. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: at least 5 subjects with Level 2 in HKDSE or equivalent, including English & Chinese languages and Mathematics, preferably a recognised degree in Human Resources Management or a relevant discipline; good communication skills in both English and Chinese (preferably including Putonghua); good service attitude and interpersonal skills; and proficiency in computer applications. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WO": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Academic Service Officer (REG) (26001WO)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Academic Service Officer (REG) (26001WO) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Academic Service Officer (REG) (26001WO) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . The Registry is a key central administrative unit of the University supporting it in providing quality higher education. We administer and deliver a broad range of student and academic services, such as admissions, registration, quality assurance, class scheduling, examinations, and graduation. The Registry is also responsible for maintaining student records and providing secretarial support to Senate and its committees, and are integral in the governing of academic regulations of the University. We provide aspiring candidates with ample staff development opportunities and a promising career in higher education. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Registry : Assistant Academic Service Officer (REG) - ( 26001WO ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Registry Closing Date : 08/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing administrative support to the day-to-day operation of the Registry, including admission, course enrolment, student administration system and enquiry services. Performing efficient and accurate clerical and administrative duties including but not limited to applications handling, course enrolment processing, tuition fee collection and record keeping; Providing professional frontline student services including counter, emails and hotline service; Assisting in the implementation and enhancement of the student administration system; Providing support to supervisor(s) in coordination and liaison with internal and external parties; Assisting supervisor(s) in the preparation of meetings, reports, publications, and student events; and Performing any other duties as assigned by supervisors. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: At least 5 passes in HKCEE or 5 subjects with Level 2 or equivalent in HKDSE, including English & Chinese languages and Mathematics; Good communication and writing skills in English and Chinese (including Putonghua); Proficient digital skills with the use of Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Chinese word processing); Capable of multi-tasking and attentive to details; and Be a good team player with strong sense of responsibility and motivation. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WD": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant II (N&HS) (26001WD)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant II (N&HS) (26001WD) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant II (N&HS) (26001WD) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences : Research Assistant II (N&HS) - ( 26001WD ) Job : Full-time R&D School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 08/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM The appointee will work under the supervision of Principal Investigator Dr Polly Ma on a research project examining the effectiveness of self-compassion interventions in improving the mental health of transgender and gender diverse individuals. Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Coordinating and participating in project activities, including participants interviews and workshop facilitation; Preparing academic and research materials, such as literature reviews, participant recruitment, data collection, quantitative and qualitative data analysis, and progress report writing; Liaising with external collaborators, including non-governmental organizations and community groups, to support project progression and management; Providing administrative support to the project team; and Undertaking any other duties as assigned by the project leader or his/her delegates. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience, and competence: A Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Psychology, Social Sciences, Gender Studies, Public Health, or other related disciplines (or equivalent qualifications); A strong research interest in working with gender minority populations; Experience with quantitative or health research methods; Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese; Excellent organizational and communication skills; and A strong sense of self-motivation and responsibility, with intellectual curiosity, critical thinking abilities, and the capacity to design and execute research independently. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary and an end-of-contract gratuity will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University's eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled. Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001W1": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Accounting Officer (Revenue) (FO) (26001W1)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Accounting Officer (Revenue) (FO) (26001W1) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Accounting Officer (Revenue) (FO) (26001W1) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Finance Office : Assistant Accounting Officer (Revenue) (FO) - ( 26001W1 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Finance Office Closing Date : 07/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Performing daily revenue collection and preparing proper accounting entries in accordance with policies and procedures; Support revenue reconciliation and assist with month-end and year-end closing processes; Coordinating with user departments or other offices/units on tuition fees collection and student-related disbursements; Professionally and promptly manage internal and student inquiries; and Performing any other duties and responsibilities as assigned by supervisors. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: At least 5 subjects with Level 2 in HKDSE or equivalent, including English & Chinese languages and Mathematics. Diploma or above in Accounting, Finance or related disciplines is highly preferred; 1 year's accounting related experience is preferred (fresh graduates will also be considered); Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, e.g. WORD, EXCEL, etc.; Experience in Oracle Finance System will be an added advantage; Good communication skills in both English and Chinese (preferably including Putonghua); Be a good team player with strong sense of responsibility and motivation; Responsible, well-organized, attentive to details and independent; and Able to work under pressure and meet tight deadlines. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001W0": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Officer (OSI) (26001W0) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Officer (OSI) (26001W0) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Office of Strategic Initiatives : Officer (OSI) - ( 26001W0 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office of Strategic Initiatives Closing Date : 07/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Vice President of the Office of Strategic Initiatives, the appointee will be part of a team supporting strategic initiatives of the University, including its advancement as a University of Applied Sciences (UAS), the expansion of strategic collaborations in the Chinese Mainland and internationally, as well as the development of executive education programmes. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing general administrative support in the development and delivery of executive education programmes and short programmes (study tours and summer/winter schools), including recruitment and enrolment; Supporting the coordination of event logistics, management of membership systems, and daily operations for programme delivery and administration; Assisting in programme promotion and participant communications, including developing marketing collaterals, updating webpages, providing student support services, and handling programme enquiries; Assisting in general administrative duties, including office management and processing payments and invoices; and Performing other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Possess a recognized degree with post-qualification work experience; prior experience in tertiary education institutions would be an advantage; Good organizational skills and attention to detail; Good interpersonal skills; An excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; and Proficiency in computer applications such as MS Word, MS Excel and English and Chinese word processing. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in May 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001VZ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Manager (OSI) (26001VZ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Manager (OSI) (26001VZ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Manager (OSI) (26001VZ) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Office of Strategic Initiatives : Assistant Manager (OSI) - ( 26001VZ ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office of Strategic Initiatives Closing Date : 07/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Vice President of the Office of Strategic Initiatives, the appointee will be part of a team supporting strategic initiatives of the University, including its advancement as a University of Applied Sciences (UAS), the expansion of strategic collaborations in the Chinese Mainland and internationally, as well as the development of executive education programmes. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing administrative support in the development and delivery of executive education programmes and short programmes (study tours and summer/winter schools), managing tasks such as recruitment, enrolment, and providing secretarial support for meetings; Assisting in the planning and execution of event logistics, membership systems, as well as other daily operations and tasks for the administration of executive education and short programmes; Supporting programme promotion and participant communications, including facilitating community building and engagement among students, alumni, as well as industry and academic partners; Facilitating the Office’s communications with both internal units and external stakeholders in the planning, development, and implementation of strategic initiatives; and Performing other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Possess a recognized degree and at least two years of relevant post-qualification work experience; prior experience in tertiary education institutions would be an advantage; Excellent organizational skills with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively; Ability to work both collaboratively and independently with internal and external parties at all levels; An excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; and Proficiency in computer applications such as MS Word, MS Excel and English and Chinese word processing. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in May 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001VY": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Manager (OSI) (26001VY) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Manager (OSI) (26001VY) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Office of Strategic Initiatives : Manager (OSI) - ( 26001VY ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office of Strategic Initiatives Closing Date : 07/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Vice President of the Office of Strategic Initiatives, the appointee will be part of a team supporting strategic initiatives of the University, including its advancement as a University of Applied Sciences (UAS), the expansion of strategic collaborations in the Chinese Mainland and internationally, as well as the development of executive education programmes. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing oversight and support for strategic initiatives, including cross-border collaborations and the development of executive education programmes; Identifying and advancing strategic partnership opportunities in the Chinese Mainland, including facilitating the development of collaborative projects and initiatives; Coordinating communication among relevant Schools and Offices within the University for the planning, development, and implementation of strategic initiatives; Managing the University’s communication and engagement with key stakeholders, particularly in the Chinese Mainland, including government authorities, industry organizations, and academic institutions; Overseeing and coordinating team efforts in supporting the Office’s functions, with particular emphasis on enhancing the University’s presence, visibility, and network within the Chinese Mainland; and Performing other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized degree, preferably a higher degree, with at least six years of relevant work experience, preferably gained in a tertiary education setting; Excellent organizational skills with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively; Ability to work both collaboratively and independently with internal and external parties at all levels; Proactiveness and devotion with strong leadership and supervisory skills; Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with high proficiency in Putonghua and written Chinese; and Proficiency in computer applications such as MS Word, MS Excel and English and Chinese word processing. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in May 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001VV": {
      "title": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) (26001VV)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) (26001VV) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) (26001VV) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences : Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) - ( 26001VV ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 06/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: undertaking course planning and development; undertaking course coordination, clinical assessments and mentoring, and classroom teaching in Nursing and related disciplines/areas; undertaking/engaging in scholarly activities/academic research and participating in School/University activities and administration; and performing any duties assigned by the Dean. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: a Master’s degree in Nursing or a related health discipline; professional registration/licensure with relevant Boards/Councils as appropriate; relevant teaching experience with at least 5 years’ of professional experience, preferably in the areas of Adult and Child Nursing or other Clinical Nursing Specialties; track record in relevant research areas where appropriate, and a good command of English and Chinese. The level of appointment depends on the candidate’s academic background, experience and competence in academic leadership, teaching, research, scholarly publications, etc. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust” Overseas candidates who are successfully appointed by the University and below age 50 will be eligible to apply for the “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust”. This programme offers the opportunity to reside in assigned accommodation free of charge for a period of up to six months, subject to terms and conditions. To Apply Please submit your application via the University’s eRecruitment System. The University will review your application and contact you should there be a suitable vacancy. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001VR": {
      "title": "Job Description - Senior Medical Laboratory Technologist (at the rank of Senior Lecturer) (N&HS)  (26001VR)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Medical Laboratory Technologist (at the rank of Senior Lecturer) (N&HS)  (26001VR) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Medical Laboratory Technologist (at the rank of Senior Lecturer) (N&HS)  (26001VR) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences: Senior Medical Laboratory Technologist (at the rank of Senior Lecturer) (N&HS) - ( 26001VR ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 04/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Performing teaching and learning activities, including preparing and developing teaching materials, delivering lecture, tutorials, and laboratory classes; Supporting all aspects of academic activities through course planning, development, coordination and delivery in related discipline(s); Providing clinical teaching to students and support clinical practicum in hospitals ; Supervising undergraduate and postgraduate research project(s); Participating in programme development and accreditation exercises; Providing training and supervising laboratory staff to prepare the necessary materials and equipment for setting up laboratory class; Writing up standard operation procedures to set-up and maintenance of equipment(s); Ensuring the safety and security related issues in the laboratories; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Dean. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: a recognised higher degree in medical laboratory science or a related discipline; Part 1 Registration and a valid practicing certificate with the Medical Laboratory Technologist Board of HKSAR; Substantial professional working experience in m edical laboratory settings, specifically in Anatomical and Cellular Pathology, Clinical Chemistry and Immunology, Haematology and Transfusion Science, or Medical Microbiology; Relevant teaching experience at tertiary level is advantages; and Strong communication skills and proficiency in using English as the medium of instruction. Fractional appointment will also be considered for successful applicant(s). Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust” Overseas candidates who are successfully appointed by the University and below age 50 will be eligible to apply for the “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust”. This programme offers the opportunity to reside in assigned accommodation free of charge for a period of up to six months, subject to terms and conditions. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
