      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (English) (LiPACE) (260021G)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (English) (LiPACE) (260021G) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (English) (LiPACE) (260021G) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education (LiPACE) As one of the eight schools of HKMU, LiPACE has a strong track record of serving diverse learner groups in Hong Kong. Established in 1992 as the Centre for Continuing and Community Education, the institution was elevated to an Institute in 2000 and officially named LiPACE. In January 2020, the University Council approved LiPACE’s normalization as a School, marking a major milestone in its development. As the designated professional and continuing education arm of the University, LiPACE is committed to providing high-quality learning opportunities with a primary focus on Vocational and Professional Education and Training (VPET). This distinctive role differentiates it from the other schools of the University, which primarily offer bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral programmes through full-time and distance learning modes. LiPACE’s academic remit and community engagement activities are organized around four key programme areas: (1) Further Education, (2) Access Programmes, (3) Professional and Continuing Education and Corporate Training, and (4) Adult Education. Beyond these core areas, LiPACE actively promotes non-formal learning in the community through targeted projects. In fulfilling the University’s founding mission of “education for all,” LiPACE complements the broader academic offerings by covering a wide range of disciplines and study levels, while serving learners of diverse ages, nationalities, and occupations. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position(s) in the LiPACE : Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (English) (LiPACE) - ( 260021G ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : Li Ka Shing School of Professional and Continuing Education Closing Date : 27/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Teaching English at Sub-degree and Diploma levels; Undertaking programme/course planning, development and coordination; Assisting instructors in course preparation and administration, conducting tutorials, grading assessments, and invigilating examinations; Supervising native English teachers to plan and design English enhancement workshops (e.g., IELTS) and employability and articulation sessions; Planning and delivering student engagement, co-curricular and extra-curricular activities; Leading and Coordinating School/Divisional projects and initiatives in line with the School’s development direction; Engaging in professional/scholarly activities; Participating in School/University activities and administration; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Dean (LiPACE) or his/her nominee. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Native or near-native fluency in English; A higher degree in English Language or a related discipline; Substantial experience in teaching English as a second language is required; Significant teaching/administration experience in tertiary/continuing education and/or significant professional experience in related subject areas is required; and Good interpersonal skills. The following qualifications/skills would be an advantage: Ability to teach additional subjects at the Diploma and Higher Diploma levels. A recognized teaching qualification (e.g., BEd, PGCE, PGDE). Proficiency in Cantonese and Mandarin. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260021J": {
      "title": "Academic Support Officer (N&HS) (260021J)",
      "description": "Job Description -  Academic Support Officer (N&HS)  (260021J) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description -  Academic Support Officer (N&HS)  (260021J) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences: Academic Support Officer (N&HS) - ( 260021J ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 25/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Planning, coordinating, and evaluating student programmes, student activities, workshops, ceremonies, and other school-level events; Preparing event proposals, budgets, promotional materials, registration forms, briefing notes, reports, and post-event evaluations; Liaising with students, faculty members, partners, travel agents, vendors, venues, and other external stakeholders; Organising overseas study tours, including itinerary planning, student recruitment, logistics, risk assessment, budget monitoring, and travel arrangements; Handling participant enquiries and maintain accurate records in accordance with University policies; Providing administrative support to committees, including organising meetings, preparing agendas and meeting papers, taking minutes, and following up on action items; Supporting evening or weekend events when necessary; and Performing other duties assigned by the Dean and supervisor. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: a recognized degree, with at least 2 years of relevant post-qualification experience, preferably in student event administration in higher education institutions ; be highly attentive to details with good organizational skills, with strong sense of responsibility and ownership; be able to work independently and proactively, and be a good team player with good communication skills; a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; proficiency in computer applications including MS Office, Chinese word processing, Canva or other tools for design; and Willingness to work outside normal office hours when required. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled ."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260021B": {
      "title": "Administration Manager (LiPACE) (260021B)",
      "description": "Job Description - Administration Manager (LiPACE) (260021B) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administration Manager (LiPACE) (260021B) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education (LiPACE) As one of the eight schools of HKMU, LiPACE has a strong track record of serving diverse learner groups in Hong Kong. Established in 1992 as the Centre for Continuing and Community Education, the institution was elevated to an Institute in 2000 and officially named LiPACE. In January 2020, the University Council approved LiPACE’s normalization as a School, marking a major milestone in its development. As the designated professional and continuing education arm of the University, LiPACE is committed to providing high-quality learning opportunities with a primary focus on Vocational and Professional Education and Training (VPET). This distinctive role differentiates it from the other schools of the University, which primarily offer bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral programmes through full-time and distance learning modes. LiPACE’s academic remit and community engagement activities are organized around four key programme areas: (1) Further Education, (2) Access Programmes, (3) Professional and Continuing Education and Corporate Training, and (4) Adult Education. Beyond these core areas, LiPACE actively promotes non-formal learning in the community through targeted projects. In fulfilling the University’s founding mission of “education for all,” LiPACE complements the broader academic offerings by covering a wide range of disciplines and study levels, while serving learners of diverse ages, nationalities, and occupations. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position(s) in the LiPACE : Administration Manager (LiPACE) - ( 260021B ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Li Ka Shing School of Professional and Continuing Education Closing Date : 24/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Contributing to the School’s administration by providing comprehensive executive support to the Dean’s Office, ensuring efficient handling of documentation, records, and administrative workflows; Coordinating meeting paper preparation and filing for the Dean’s Office; Managing Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) and agreement records, supporting MOU signing ceremonies, membership fee processing, and study visit arrangements; Overseeing the planning of School‑level events and functions to ensure proper execution; Maintaining daily document control records and monitoring administrative databases; Supervising and guiding junior staff to uphold effective administrative services; Providing executive support to School working groups and special projects; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Dean (LiPACE) or his/her nominee(s). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized degree, preferably a higher degree, with at least 2 years of relevant post‑qualification experience; Excellent interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills; Demonstrated ability to be flexible and adaptable, with a commitment to respond proactively to rapidly changing needs; Proven ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment; High level of competence in written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); Strong computer literacy and numeracy skills, with proficiency in office software and document management systems; and Demonstrated ability to supervise junior staff and foster a collaborative team environment. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600214": {
      "title": "Academic Service Manager (Admissions Enrolment (Distance Learning) & Communications) (REG)",
      "description": "Job Description - Academic Service Manager (Admissions Enrolment (Distance Learning) & Communications) (REG) (2600214) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Academic Service Manager (Admissions Enrolment (Distance Learning) & Communications) (REG) (2600214) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . The Registry is a key central administrative unit of the University supporting it in providing quality higher education. We administer and deliver a broad range of student and academic services, such as admissions, registration, quality assurance, class scheduling, examinations, and graduation. The Registry is also responsible for maintaining student records and providing secretarial support to Senate and its committees, and are integral in the governing of academic regulations of the University. We provide aspiring candidates with ample staff development opportunities and a promising career in higher education. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Registry : Academic Service Manager (Admissions Enrolment (Distance Learning) & Communications) (REG) - ( 2600214 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Registry Closing Date : 27/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will play a key role in the Distance Learning team and Communications team of the Registry, and will be mainly responsible for the following tasks: Overseeing the administration of Distance Learning programmes and courses, including admissions, enrolments, websites, and publications; Developing and executing new initiatives to streamline work processes and improve operational workflows through system enhancements Managing communication channels such as website content, announcements, emails, kiosks and counter services to engage current students; Delivering timely current student communications through the mapping of student lifecycle and events for contributing to the success of the overall student journey and experience; Providing the continuous support and improvement of smart locker system, digital queuing system and chatbot with usage tracking, statistical reporting and feedback collection; Supervising executive and clerical staff, and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized degree with 6 years’ post-qualification experience, preference will be given to those with experience in student services in tertiary institutions; Strong project management and execution abilities, resilient and flexible in dealing with emergency and ambiguity; Good leadership and management skills, strong interpersonal and organizational skills while with servicing and collaborating mindsets; A high sense of self-motivation and ownership, a problem solver, capability to work under pressure; Strong system sense and good computer skills including MS Office; Excellent command of English and Chinese, including Putonghua; and Work outside office hours may be required. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in May 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
