    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260020B": {
      "title": "Manager (Business Development) (ALTO) (260020B)",
      "description": "Job Description - Manager (Business Development) (ALTO) (260020B) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Manager (Business Development) (ALTO) (260020B) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the InnoLearn Hub Limited: Manager (Business Development) (ALTO) - ( 260020B ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office for Advancement of Learning and Teaching Closing Date : 21/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will serve as the Business Development Manager of the newly established InnoLearn Hub Limited, playing a pivotal role in the commercialization and market expansion of the online English learning platforms developed by the University. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Developing and executing competitive marketing, promotional strategies and business development plans tailored to the characteristics of the platforms; Leading outreach and engagement with School Principals, English Panel Teachers, conducting workshops and demonstrations of the platforms to the primary and secondary schools; Representing the company in promoting the online learning platforms by conducting, and/or participating in exhibitions, conferences, and education-related expos; Collaborating with internal teams and relevant stakeholders to ensure smooth implementation and promotion of the platforms; Analyzing market trends and competitor activities to identify business opportunities with primary and secondary schools, private schools, learning centres and educational institutions in Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area to expand the reach of the deliverables and ensure long-term sustainability; Preparing and presenting comprehensive reports on marketing plans and performance to senior management, and providing insights on business operations to support better marketing and promotional strategies; and Providing administrative and operational support, and performing any other duties as assigned by the supervisor(s). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized degree, preferably a higher degree, in Marketing, Communication, English, Educational Technology, or a related discipline; Substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience, preferably with proven track record in planning and executing marketing strategies for online learning platforms or education-related products in educational settings are preferred; Experience in working with primary and/or secondary schools in Hong Kong, including engaging with School Principals, English teachers and curriculum coordinators; Prior experience in English teaching at primary and/or secondary levels in Hong Kong is highly preferred; Experience in organising and participating in education-related expos, exhibitions, conferences or large-scale promotional events, and in delivering school-based training, demonstrations, seminars and workshops for teachers and students will be an advantage; Exposure to the private primary and/or secondary schools and learning centres in Hong Kong and/or the education market in the Greater Bay Area will be a strong advantage; D eep understanding of Hong Kong primary and secondary school curricula and assessment practices (e.g. the English Language Curriculum (Key stages 1 to 3) and the PIRLS framework); Excellent interpersonal, communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills; An excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to participate in a trade test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment Successful candidate will be appointed on a 2-year full-time contract on project basis. An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidate. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001WP": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst (Web) (ITO) (26001WP)",
      "description": "Job Description - Systems Analyst (Web) (ITO) (26001WP) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Systems Analyst (Web) (ITO) (26001WP) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Information Technology Office : Systems Analyst (Web) (ITO) - ( 26001WP ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Information Technology Office Closing Date : 21/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Systems Analyst (Web) Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Developing, maintaining, and supporting backend components for the University’s web services and WordPress-based platforms; Maintaining and optimizing MySQL databases, including performance tuning, query optimization, indexing, and routine database maintenance; Supporting WordPress plugin development, customization, upgrades, testing, and troubleshooting; Developing and integrating APIs for web applications, third-party systems, and internal services; Assisting in the administration and optimization of related database tools and backend utilities; Supporting website stability, scalability, and performance through monitoring, troubleshooting, and technical improvements; Assisting in cloud-based hosting and deployment tasks, with exposure to Microsoft Azure environments; Applying security best practices in system design, access control, patching, and vulnerability mitigation; Participating in stress testing, load testing, and performance validation to ensure web service reliability; Working closely with frontend, infrastructure, and content teams to deliver secure and efficient web solutions; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a related discipline; At least 3 years of relevant post-qualification experience in backend development, database administration, or web application support; Solid hands-on experience with - WordPress plugin development, customization, and upgrade support; - API development, integration, and troubleshooting; - PHP, SQL, Python and related backend technologies; - MySQL database maintenance, tuning, optimization, and troubleshooting; - Microsoft Azure knowledge or cloud platform exposure; - Website stress testing, performance testing, and service reliability validation; - Security concepts and best practices in web and database environments; Experience in WordPress environments and enterprise web systems would be an advantage; Familiarity with logging, monitoring, and incident troubleshooting in production systems; Good analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills; A good team player who is proactive, detail-oriented, and able to work independently; and Good communication skills in both English and Chinese. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600203": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I / II (R6860) (S&T)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant I / II (R6860) (S&T) (2600203) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant I / II (R6860) (S&T) (2600203) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Science and Technology: Research Assistant I / II (R6860) (S&T) - ( 2600203 ) Job : Full-time R&D School/Unit : School of Science and Technology Closing Date : 20/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will mainly assist the research team in a research project \"A Novel Vision Transformer-Based Neural Network for Image Classification and Jet Tagging in Lepton-Flavor Violating Processes\" (R6860). He / She will be responsible mainly for the following: Collecting and preprocessing data for machine learning model training; Developing AI models, both by adapting existing frameworks and building architectures from scratch; Evaluating and benchmarking model performance; Conducting literature reviews by searching and synthesizing recent journal articles; and Performing any other research or administrative duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator(s) or Supervisor(s). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A master’s degree or above in Physics, Data Science, Computer Science, or a related discipline (for Research Assistant I) ; A bachelor’s degree or above in Physics, Data Science, Computer Science, or a related discipline (for Research Assistant II) ; Good command of written and verbal communication skills; fluency in English is preferred, while knowledge of Cantonese and Putonghua is not essential; Proven experience in deep learning model development, including designing neural network architectures from scratch, is essential; Solid foundational knowledge of Python programming is required; high proficiency will be a distinct advantage; A basic understanding of high-energy physics will be an advantage; and Prior research experience with CERN or other particle collider experiments will be considered an absolute advantage. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary and an end-of-contract gratuity, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in July 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260020A": {
      "title": "Associate Director (LiPACE) (260020A)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Director (LiPACE) (260020A) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Director (LiPACE) (260020A) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education (LiPACE) As one of the eight schools of HKMU, LiPACE has a strong track record of serving diverse learner groups in Hong Kong. Established in 1992 as the Centre for Continuing and Community Education, the institution was elevated to an Institute in 2000 and officially named LiPACE. In January 2020, the University Council approved LiPACE’s normalization as a School, marking a major milestone in its development. As the designated professional and continuing education arm of the University, LiPACE is committed to providing high-quality learning opportunities with a primary focus on Vocational and Professional Education and Training (VPET). This distinctive role differentiates it from the other schools of the University, which primarily offer bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral programmes through full-time and distance learning modes. LiPACE’s academic remit and community engagement activities are organized around four key programme areas: (1) Further Education, (2) Access Programmes, (3) Professional and Continuing Education and Corporate Training, and (4) Adult Education. Beyond these core areas, LiPACE actively promotes non-formal learning in the community through targeted projects. In fulfilling the University’s founding mission of “education for all,” LiPACE complements the broader academic offerings by covering a wide range of disciplines and study levels, while serving learners of diverse ages, nationalities, and occupations. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position(s) in the LiPACE : Associate Director (LiPACE) - ( 260020A ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : Li Ka Shing School of Professional and Continuing Education Closing Date : 20/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Dean of Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education, the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Assisting the Dean in the overall management of the School; Providing academic leadership and guidance for the planning, development, delivery and quality assurance of programmes and courses; Supervising administrative units and academic divisions; Assisting the Dean to implement collaborations and projects with external partners; Engaging in scholarly and professional activities; Participating in School/University activities and administration; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Dean (LiPACE). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A higher degree (preferably an earned doctorate) and professional qualification in relevant areas; Substantial teaching/management experience in tertiary/post-secondary/continuing and professional education and professional experience in the related subject; Having strong ability to build rapport with a broad spectrum of stakeholders; Active involvement in scholarly, professional and community activities is required; and Excellent interpersonal skills and be proficient in English & Chinese languages (preferably including Putonghua). Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful."
    },
