    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260022O": {
      "title": "Manager, MIAO (International) (260022O)",
      "description": "Job Description - Manager, MIAO (International) (260022O) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Manager, MIAO (International) (260022O) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Mainland and International Affairs Office. Manager, MIAO (International) - ( 260022O ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Mainland and International Affairs Office Closing Date : 01/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of the Mainland and International Affairs Office (MIAO), the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Implementing Partnership Strategies: Develop and execute action plans to forge partnerships with universities. This involves conducting research and analysis of markets and universities, as well as monitoring trends and developments in international higher education to identify opportunities for the HKMU community. Managing International Student Recruitment: Source and evaluate potential student recruitment partners, manage partner networks, and deliver training to ensure compliance with HKMU's policies. Execute international student recruitment plan for prioritized regions in the global market. Manage partnerships with service providers, agencies, and schools within these regions, and being accountable for the recruitment pipeline that ultimately leads to the enrollment of international students at our university. Supporting Management on External Engagements: Provide support to management regarding HKMU's external engagements, including managing incoming visits from partners and higher education institutions, as well as supporting student mobility missions. Providing executive and team support to the Mainland and International Affairs Office, as well as related committees and working groups; and Performing any other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Mainland and International Affairs or his/her delegate(s). The position requires practical knowledge of marketing and sales within the international education sector. This may include student recruitment through service provider networks, direct engagement with schools and other providers to foster long-term relationships, and supporting direct recruitment strategies and execution in the designated territory. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A bachelor’s degree and at least 6 years of experience in partnership development within higher education and international student recruitment, particularly in sourcing and managing international student recruitment partners. Experience in Southeast Asia and/or Central Asia is a plus; A proven track record of strong marketing and sales performance; Demonstrated ability to identify and pursue partnership and international student recruitment opportunities that align with the university’s strategic objectives; Strong interpersonal, communication, and negotiation skills in business-level English and Chinese (including Mandarin), both written and spoken. Proficiency in an additional Southeast Asian or Central Asian language (such as Thai, Bahasa, Uzbek, or Kazakh) is a plus; A solid understanding of the international education industry and the ability to navigate multicultural settings effectively;and A flexible attitude toward work, including a willingness to work weekends and evenings to support recruitment activities both locally and internationally. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260022K": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260022K)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260022K) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260022K) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Library : Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) - ( 260022K ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Library Closing Date : 04/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Assisting in overseeing daily operations of the Library Systems and Technology Section; Assisting in planning, coordinating, and managing activities related to library systems and technology; Assisting in formulating policies and procedures related to library systems and technology; Assisting in administering the Alma integrated library system, link resolver, Primo discovery portal, and other digital systems of the Library; Assisting in developing and maintaining the Library’s application programmes and database systems; Serving on committees and task forces as appropriate; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the University Librarian or his/her nominee. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree; At least 2 years’ relevant post-qualification experience (for Assistant Manager); Substantial relevant post-qualification experience in library systems in an academic library is advantageous; Hands-on experience in managing software, hardware running various operating systems, and networking is advantageous; Working knowledge of HTML, XML, Java, JavaScript, CSS, PHP, MySQL, etc. is preferred; and Good interpersonal and communication skills in both English and Chinese. Applicants with less relevant experience may be considered for appointment as Library Officer. Candidates with a professional library qualification (e.g., AALIA, ALA, MCLIP, MLIS or equivalent) may be appointed as Assistant Librarian II, commensurate with work experience. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in October 2025 - June 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600230": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst (OPA)",
      "description": "Job Description - Systems Analyst (OPA) (2600230) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Systems Analyst (OPA) (2600230) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Office of Planning and Analysis : Systems Analyst (OPA) - ( 2600230 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office of Planning and Analysis Closing Date : 01/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Translating complex functional business rules and user requirements into comprehensive specifications, database schema designs, and system workflow diagrams; Designing, developing, and managing APIs and system integrations, ensuring solutions are scalable, secure, and aligned with requirements and standards; Collaborating with project teams to develop test strategies, oversee testing phases, and resolve defects to meet quality benchmarks; Authoring user documentation, delivering system training workshops, and providing ongoing post-implementation support; Auditing system outputs for accuracy, collecting user feedback, and implementing continuous platform enhancements; and Undertaking other duties as assigned by the Director of the Office of Planning and Analysis. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related quantitative field; Minimum 2 years of experience as a Systems Analyst, Analyst Programmer, or Software Engineer; Demonstrated experience in user requirement gathering, systems analysis, and technical documentation; Strong knowledge of relational database design, data modelling, and SQL (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server); Hands-on full-stack development experience with: (i) Backend technologies and frameworks (e.g., Python/Django, Node.js); (ii) Frontend web technologies (e.g., React, JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap); and (iii) RESTful API design, microservices architecture, and data integration. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in both English and Chinese; Proven analytical, diagnostic, and problem-solving capabilities; and Familiarity with Microsoft Dynamics 365 or enterprise CRM/ERP solutions is a definite plus. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in July 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
