      "title": "Project Officer (OPA) (260022Y)",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Officer (OPA) (260022Y) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Officer (OPA) (260022Y) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Office of Planning and Analysis : Project Officer (OPA) - ( 260022Y ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Office of Planning and Analysis Closing Date : 01/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Handling daily clerical work, phone/email inquiries, document filing, and meeting logistics (scheduling, room setup, and drafting minutes); Acting as the contact point between OPA and other offices; assisting with user requirement gathering, User Acceptance Testing (UAT), user guides, and frontline user support; Performing accurate data entry, record updates, and data cleansing for university address and analytics systems; and Undertaking other duties as assigned by the Director of the Office of Planning and Analysis. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Bachelor’s degree in any discipline; At least 1-2 years of experience in office administration or project coordination; Hands-on ability to use Microsoft Excel and Word to organise data and prepare reports; Detail-oriented, organised, and a good team player; and Good communication skills in both English and Chinese (written and spoken). Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in July 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260022Z": {
      "title": "Assistant Facilities Manager (Building Services) (FMO) (260022Z)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Facilities Manager (Building Services) (FMO) (260022Z) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Facilities Manager (Building Services) (FMO) (260022Z) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Facilities Management Office : Assistant Facilities Manager (Building Services) (FMO) - ( 260022Z ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Facilities Management Office Closing Date : 02/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Conducting in‑house feasibility studies and providing professional advice on building services solutions that meet the required quality, safety and regulatory standards; Coordinating with in‑house designers and producing detailed MVAC, FS, P&D, ELV and electrical designs, calculations, specifications and drawings for tender issuance, using industry‑standard CAD and BIM software; Reviewing designs and outputs prepared by external consultants, and contractors' submissions (including shop drawings, equipment schedules, installation details and method statements), to ensure compliance with design intent, statutory requirements and industry standards, and providing recommendations to the project team; Ensuring fully integrated and coordinated MEP design with architectural, structural and other disciplines, including interfaces with builder's works, site possession and access arrangements; Overseeing assigned projects from design through construction to handover, managing timelines, budgets and resources to ensure timely and cost‑effective delivery to the required quality; Monitoring project expenditure and progress through effective project and construction management techniques, and ensuring adherence to building regulations, safety requirements and industry standards; Reviewing technical proposals and site works to ensure the required quality and safety standards are maintained; Taking a leading role in the supervision of installation and testing and commissioning (T&C) of building services and equipment, working closely with contractors on the preparation, planning and implementation of the works; Carrying out site inspections and quality checks to verify that installation work meets design specifications and standards; Preparing pre‑commissioning checklists, T&C procedures, acceptance criteria and commissioning sequences for critical equipment, and assisting in the formulation of the overall commissioning programme in line with project key dates; Providing technical support and resolving engineering issues during the installation and commissioning phases; Liaising with government authorities, consultants, contractors, architects and internal parties on project requirements and progress; Collaborating with stakeholders and in‑house specialists to ensure user requirements are met and projects are successfully delivered; Maintaining comprehensive records and preparing technical documentation, drawings, reports and regular progress reports; and Performing any other duties as assigned by supervisors. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Electrical Engineering, Building Services Engineering or a related discipline; Preferably corporate membership of the Hong Kong Institution of Engineers (MHKIE) or equivalent; At least 5 years' relevant post‑qualification experience in the design, construction, operation and maintenance of building services installations; Proven experience in handling medium to large‑scale education, institutional, hostel, office or asset enhancement projects; Solid experience in new building and fit‑out design, production of schematic drawings, and tender preparation and assessment; Excellent knowledge of building services engineering, covering design, installation, operation and maintenance; Familiarity with building regulations and related statutory requirements; Strong leadership and project management skills, with good analytical, negotiation and organisational abilities; Excellent communication, presentation and interpersonal skills, with a service mindset; Proficiency in MS Office applications and AutoCAD; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; knowledge of Putonghua is an advantage; Proactive, self‑motivated team player with strong attention to detail and the ability to perform under pressure; Preference will be given to candidates with building services experience gained in both developer and consultancy firms; and Knowledge and experience in BIM will be an added advantage. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260022X": {
      "title": "Facilities Manager (Contract & Cost Management) (FMO) (260022X)",
      "description": "Job Description - Facilities Manager (Contract & Cost Management) (FMO) (260022X) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Facilities Manager (Contract & Cost Management) (FMO) (260022X) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Facilities Management Office : Facilities Manager (Contract & Cost Management) (FMO) - ( 260022X ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Facilities Management Office Closing Date : 02/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities T he appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Reviewing and establishing in‑house, project‑wide standards for cost planning and budget control, and developing monitoring mechanisms to track expenditure, flag variances and support timely management intervention across all projects; Formulating comprehensive budgets and cost plans, and preparing detailed cost estimates and analyses for new works, subcontracting, variation works and minor/maintenance projects; Monitoring project expenditure against approved budgets and advising the project team on cost‑effective and value‑added solutions; Reviewing existing systems, tendering processes and pricing strategies to ensure optimal cost‑effectiveness; Preparing estimates, specifications and tender documents; Carrying out pre‑qualification and selection of consultants and contractors; Managing the tendering process for works, supplies and subletting of contracts, and preparing tender analyses, reports and recommendations to the Tender Board or other appropriate authorities; Participating in the selection and appointment of consultants and contractors; Carrying out measurement of works and valuation of interim payments and variations; Checking quotations, variations, payment bills and claims, and overseeing final account settlements; Liaising and coordinating with consultants on contract administration matters; Managing and supervising the performance of consultant quantity surveying firms and contractors in cost and contractual aspects; Liaising with government authorities, consultants, contractors and internal parties on project progress; Providing professional advice and recommendations to facilitate management discussions and decision‑making; Maintaining comprehensive project records and preparing regular progress and cost reports; Implementing proper control procedures to ensure full compliance with established University guidelines and policies; Assisting the Quantity Surveying Manager in the implementation, monitoring and supervision of critical assignments; and Performing any other duties as assigned by supervisors. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Quantity Surveying, Construction Economics or a related discipline; Corporate membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Surveyors (MHKIS) in the Quantity Surveying Division, or equivalent; At least 10 years' relevant post‑qualification experience in quantity surveying, contract administration and cost management; Proven experience in handling medium to large‑scale education, institutional, hostel, office or asset enhancement projects; Solid experience in tender preparation and assessment; Strong technical knowledge of measurement, cost estimating, construction technology, contracts and construction law; Familiarity with building regulations and related statutory requirements; Strong leadership and project management skills, with the ability to lead and manage teams, consultants and contractors and to handle a complex and varied workload; Excellent communication, presentation and interpersonal skills, with a service mindset; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; Self‑motivated team player with strong attention to detail and the ability to perform under pressure; Preference will be given to candidates with quantity surveying experience gained in both developer and consultancy firms; and Proficiency in AutoCAD and MS Office applications is a plus. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    }
